meta {
  name: Get Access Token
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{auth_base_url}}/auth/api/get-token
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "api_key": "{{process.env.PLYTIX_DEV_API_KEY}}",
    "api_password": "{{process.env.PLYTIX_DEV_API_PASSWORD}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data[0].access_token: isString
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    bru.setVar("access_token", res.body.data[0].access_token);
  }
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-08-31 against the "API Docs" test account
  (writechoice_test, ADMIN role) provisioned for this engagement.
  
  ## What it does
  Exchanges an account's `api_key`/`api_password` (issued by an account
  admin under the account's admin section -> "API" tab) for a short-lived
  Bearer access token used on every subsequent PIM API call.
  
  ## Confirmed behavior (differs from the v1 Postman collection's docs)
  - Response `data[0]` includes an undocumented `refresh_token` field
    alongside `access_token`. No refresh-token endpoint is documented
    anywhere in the collection or `API V3.md` -- unclear whether it is
    usable, or a leftover/future field. Value observed was a placeholder-
    looking string, not a real JWT.
  - `access_token` is a JWT. Decoded payload confirms: 15-minute lifetime
    (`exp` - `iat` = 900s, matching the product team's statement in the
    2026-08-31 kickoff call), and embeds the full user/account/permissions
    object (`user_claims`) -- account id, role, and a granular
    `pim_permissions` map. Useful context, but nothing in the docs
    mentions the token is this information-dense.
  - Response headers include rate-limit info not documented anywhere:
    `ratelimit-limit: 8`, `x-ratelimit-limit-second: 8` on this endpoint
    specifically (separate from the higher per-account PIM rate limits
    embedded in the JWT's `account.rate_limit` claim: 20 req/10s and
    15000 req/3600s).
  
  ## Required fields
  | Field | Type | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | api_key | string | from account admin -> API tab |
  | api_password | string | from account admin -> API tab |
  
  ## Using the token
  `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` on all subsequent requests.
  Casing of "Bearer" and the single space matter (per the collection's own
  docs) -- not independently re-verified this session, taken as given.
}
